IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa5-director-liabilities.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 10, Chapter 7, "Directors' liabilities": ss 232 to 239 (lines 3073-3178 of ukpga-2006-46.txt):
-- provisions protecting directors from liability (ss 232 to 238) and ratification of acts giving rise to liability (s 239).
--
-- SOURCE: a plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; not the official text.
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: see coa5-loans-exceptions.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING as the rule of 2026-10-29 reads them).
-- OFFENCES and PENALTIES: as in coa5-service-contracts.l4 (s 1121's "in default" is an input; the pounds of a standard-scale level are inputs).

§ `Chapter 7: provision protecting directors from liability (ss 232 to 238)`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 232 Provisions protecting directors from liability
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:3076 | (1) Any provision that purports to exempt a director of a company (to any extent) from any liability that would otherwise attach to him in connection with any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company is void.
@ref s 232(1) provisions exempting a director from liability (src:3076-3076)
GIVEN `the provision purports to exempt a director of a company (to any extent) from a liability that would otherwise attach to him in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(1) the provision is void` MEANS
    IF `the provision purports to exempt a director of a company (to any extent) from a liability that would otherwise attach to him in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any provision that purports to exempt a director of a company (to any extent) from any liability that would otherwise attach to him in connection with any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company is void"

-- src:3077 | (2) Any provision by which a company directly or indirectly provides an indemnity (to any extent) for a director of the company, or of an associated company, against any liability attaching to him in connection with any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company of which he is a director is void, except as permitted by—
-- src:3078 | (a) section 233 (provision of insurance),
-- src:3079 | (b) section 234 (qualifying third party indemnity provision), or
-- src:3080 | (c) section 235 (qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision).
@ref s 232(2) provisions indemnifying a director (src:3077-3080)
GIVEN `the company directly or indirectly provides an indemnity (to any extent)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for a director of the company, or of an associated company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `against a liability attaching to him in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company of which he is a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 233 the insurance is permitted` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 234(1) the provision is permitted as qualifying third party indemnity provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 235(1) the provision is permitted as qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(2) the provision is void` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the company directly or indirectly provides an indemnity (to any extent)` AND `for a director of the company, or of an associated company` AND `against a liability attaching to him in connection with negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company of which he is a director`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any provision by which a company directly or indirectly provides an indemnity (to any extent) for a director of the company, or of an associated company, against any liability attaching to him in connection with any negligence, default, breach of duty or breach of trust in relation to the company of which he is a director"
        IF `s 233 the insurance is permitted` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 234(1) the provision is permitted as qualifying third party indemnity provision` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 235(1) the provision is permitted as qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is void, except as permitted by— (a) section 233 (provision of insurance), (b) section 234 (qualifying third party indemnity provision), or (c) section 235 (qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision)"
        IF `s 233 the insurance is permitted` EQUALS NOTHING AND `s 234(1) the provision is permitted as qualifying third party indemnity provision` EQUALS NOTHING AND `s 235(1) the provision is permitted as qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a permission of ss 233 to 235 is answered JUST FALSE or unknown (an unmet qualifying requirement is those sections' own answer)

DECLARE `s 232(3) where the provision is found` IS ONE OF
    `s 232(3) in the company's articles`
    `s 232(3) in a contract with the company`
    `s 232(3) otherwise`

-- src:3081 | (3) This section applies to any provision, whether contained in a company's articles or in any contract with the company or otherwise.
@ref s 232(3) wherever the provision is contained (src:3081-3081)
GIVEN where IS A `s 232(3) where the provision is found`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(3) this section applies to the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER where
    WHEN `s 232(3) in the company's articles` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 232(3) in a contract with the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 232(3) otherwise` THEN JUST TRUE -- "or otherwise"

-- src:3082 | (4) Nothing in this section prevents a company's articles from making such provision as has previously been lawful for dealing with conflicts of interest.
@ref s 232(4) conflicts of interest (src:3082-3082)
GIVEN `the articles make such provision for dealing with conflicts of interest as has previously been lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 232(4) this section prevents the articles from making the provision` MEANS
    IF `the articles make such provision for dealing with conflicts of interest as has previously been lawful`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section prevents a company's articles from making such provision as has previously been lawful for dealing with conflicts of interest"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such provision as has previously been lawful for dealing with conflicts of interest"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 233 Provision of insurance
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:3084 | Section 232(2) (voidness of provisions for indemnifying directors) does not prevent a company from purchasing and maintaining for a director of the company, or of an associated company, insurance against any such liability as is mentioned in that subsection.
@ref s 233 insurance (src:3084-3084)
GIVEN `the company purchases and maintains insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for a director of the company, or of an associated company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `against a liability mentioned in section 232(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 233 the insurance is permitted` MEANS
    IF `the company purchases and maintains insurance` AND `for a director of the company, or of an associated company` AND `against a liability mentioned in section 232(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 232(2) ... does not prevent a company from purchasing and maintaining for a director of the company, or of an associated company, insurance against any such liability as is mentioned in that subsection"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 234 Qualifying third party indemnity provision
-- ======================================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 234(6) provision for relief` IS ONE OF
    `s 234(6) section 661(3) or (4)`
    `s 234(6) section 1157`
    `s 234(6) some other provision`

-- src:3105 | (6) The reference in subsection (3)(b)(iii) to an application for relief is to an application for relief under—
-- src:3106 | section 661(3) or (4) (power of court to grant relief in case of acquisition of shares by innocent nominee), or
-- src:3107 | section 1157 (general power of court to grant relief in case of honest and reasonable conduct).
@ref s 234(6) application for relief (src:3105-3107)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 234(6) provision for relief`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(6) the application is an application for relief` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 234(6) section 661(3) or (4)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 234(6) section 1157` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 234(6) some other provision` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The reference in subsection (3)(b)(iii) to an application for relief is to an application for relief under— section 661(3) or (4) ..., or section 1157"

-- src:3099 | (a) a conviction, judgment or refusal of relief becomes final—
-- src:3100 | (i) if not appealed against, at the end of the period for bringing an appeal, or
-- src:3101 | (ii) if appealed against, at the time when the appeal (or any further appeal) is disposed of; and
@ref s 234(5)(a) when a conviction, judgment or refusal of relief becomes final (src:3099-3101)
GIVEN `the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief is appealed against` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date when the period for bringing an appeal ends` IS A DATE
      `the date when the appeal (or any further appeal) is disposed of` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 234(5)(a) the date when the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief becomes final` MEANS
    IF `the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief is appealed against`
    THEN `the date when the appeal (or any further appeal) is disposed of`
    ELSE `the date when the period for bringing an appeal ends`

-- src:3102 | (b) an appeal is disposed of—
-- src:3103 | (i) if it is determined and the period for bringing any further appeal has ended, or
-- src:3104 | (ii) if it is abandoned or otherwise ceases to have effect.
@ref s 234(5)(b) when an appeal is disposed of (src:3102-3104)
GIVEN determined IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period for bringing any further appeal has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `abandoned or otherwise ceased to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(5)(b) the appeal is disposed of` MEANS
    IF (determined AND `the period for bringing any further appeal has ended`) OR `abandoned or otherwise ceased to have effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) an appeal is disposed of— (i) if it is determined and the period for bringing any further appeal has ended, or (ii) if it is abandoned or otherwise ceases to have effect"

-- src:3097 | (4) The references in subsection (3)(b) to a conviction, judgment or refusal of relief are to the final decision in the proceedings.
@ref s 234(4) the final decision (src:3097-3097)
GIVEN `the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief is the final decision in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(4) the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief counts for subsection (3)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the conviction, judgment or refusal of relief is the final decision in the proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The references in subsection (3)(b) to a conviction, judgment or refusal of relief are to the final decision in the proceedings"

-- (3): "The provision must not provide any indemnity against" the five liabilities. The facts about convictions, judgments and refusals are about final decisions ((4), (5)).
-- src:3089 | (3) The provision must not provide any indemnity against—
-- src:3090 | (a) any liability of the director to pay—
-- src:3091 | (i) a fine imposed in criminal proceedings, or
-- src:3092 | (ii) a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with any requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising); or
-- src:3093 | (b) any liability incurred by the director—
-- src:3094 | (i) in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted, or
-- src:3095 | (ii) in defending civil proceedings brought by the company, or an associated company, in which judgment is given against him, or
-- src:3096 | (iii) in connection with an application for relief (see subsection (6)) in which the court refuses to grant him relief.
@ref s 234(3) liabilities the provision must not indemnify (src:3089-3096)
GIVEN `it indemnifies a fine imposed in criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it indemnifies a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending civil proceedings brought by the company, or an associated company, in which judgment is given against him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it indemnifies a liability incurred in connection with an application for relief in which the court refuses to grant him relief` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(3) the provision provides no indemnity against the excluded liabilities` MEANS
    IF    `it indemnifies a fine imposed in criminal proceedings`
       OR `it indemnifies a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)`
       OR `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted`
       OR `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending civil proceedings brought by the company, or an associated company, in which judgment is given against him`
       OR `it indemnifies a liability incurred in connection with an application for relief in which the court refuses to grant him relief`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provision must not provide any indemnity against— (a) any liability of the director to pay— (i) a fine imposed in criminal proceedings, or (ii) a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty ...; or (b) any liability incurred by the director— (i) in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted, or (ii) ... (iii) ..."
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:3087 | (2) Third party indemnity provision means provision for indemnity against liability incurred by the director to a person other than the company or an associated company.
@ref s 234(2) third party indemnity provision (src:3087-3087)
GIVEN `it is provision for indemnity against liability incurred by the director to a person other than the company or an associated company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(2) the provision is third party indemnity provision` MEANS
    IF `it is provision for indemnity against liability incurred by the director to a person other than the company or an associated company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Third party indemnity provision means provision for indemnity against liability incurred by the director to a person other than the company or an associated company"

-- src:3088 | Such provision is qualifying third party indemnity provision if the following requirements are met.
@ref s 234(2) qualifying third party indemnity provision (src:3088-3088)
GIVEN `s 234(2) the provision is third party indemnity provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 234(3) the provision provides no indemnity against the excluded liabilities` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(2) the provision is qualifying third party indemnity provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 234(2) the provision is third party indemnity provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 234(3) the provision provides no indemnity against the excluded liabilities` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Such provision is qualifying third party indemnity provision if the following requirements are met"
        IF `s 234(2) the provision is third party indemnity provision` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 234(3) the provision provides no indemnity against the excluded liabilities` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer is not known

-- src:3086 | (1) Section 232(2) (voidness of provisions for indemnifying directors) does not apply to qualifying third party indemnity provision.
@ref s 234(1) section 232(2) does not apply to qualifying third party indemnity provision (src:3086-3086)
GIVEN `s 234(2) the provision is qualifying third party indemnity provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 234(1) the provision is permitted as qualifying third party indemnity provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 234(2) the provision is qualifying third party indemnity provision`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 232(2) ... does not apply to qualifying third party indemnity provision" (it says nothing of other provision)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the provision qualifies is not known

