    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) an appeal is disposed of— (i) if it is determined and the period for bringing any further appeal has ended, or (ii) if it is abandoned or otherwise ceases to have effect"

-- src:3117 | (4) The reference in subsection (3)(b) to a conviction is to the final decision in the proceedings.
@ref s 235(4) the final decision (src:3117-3117)
GIVEN `the conviction is the final decision in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 235(4) the conviction counts for subsection (3)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the conviction is the final decision in the proceedings`
