-- src:3112 | (3) The provision must not provide any indemnity against—
-- src:3113 | (a) any liability of the director to pay—
-- src:3114 | (i) a fine imposed in criminal proceedings, or
-- src:3115 | (ii) a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with any requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising); or
-- src:3116 | (b) any liability incurred by the director in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted.
@ref s 235(3) liabilities the provision must not indemnify (src:3112-3116)
GIVEN `it indemnifies a fine imposed in criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it indemnifies a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 235(3) the provision provides no indemnity against the excluded liabilities` MEANS
    IF    `it indemnifies a fine imposed in criminal proceedings`
       OR `it indemnifies a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty in respect of non-compliance with a requirement of a regulatory nature (however arising)`
       OR `it indemnifies a liability incurred in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provision must not provide any indemnity against— (a) any liability of the director to pay— (i) a fine imposed in criminal proceedings, or (ii) a sum payable to a regulatory authority by way of a penalty ...; or (b) any liability incurred by the director in defending criminal proceedings in which he is convicted"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:3110 | (2) Pension scheme indemnity provision means provision indemnifying a director of a company that is a trustee of an occupational pension scheme against liability incurred in connection with the company's activities as trustee of the scheme.
@ref s 235(2) pension scheme indemnity provision (src:3110-3110)
GIVEN `s 235(6) the scheme is an occupational pension scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is a trustee of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is provision indemnifying a director of the company against liability incurred in connection with the company's activities as trustee of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 235(2) the provision is pension scheme indemnity provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 235(6) the scheme is an occupational pension scheme` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the scheme is an occupational pension scheme is not known
        IF `s 235(6) the scheme is an occupational pension scheme` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the company is a trustee of the scheme` AND `it is provision indemnifying a director of the company against liability incurred in connection with the company's activities as trustee of the scheme`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Pension scheme indemnity provision means provision indemnifying a director of a company that is a trustee of an occupational pension scheme against liability incurred in connection with the company's activities as trustee of the scheme"

-- src:3111 | Such provision is qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision if the following requirements are met.
@ref s 235(2) qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision (src:3111-3111)
GIVEN `s 235(2) the provision is pension scheme indemnity provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 235(3) the provision provides no indemnity against the excluded liabilities` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 235(2) the provision is qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 235(2) the provision is pension scheme indemnity provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 235(3) the provision provides no indemnity against the excluded liabilities` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Such provision is qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision if the following requirements are met"
        IF `s 235(2) the provision is pension scheme indemnity provision` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 235(3) the provision provides no indemnity against the excluded liabilities` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer is not known

-- src:3109 | (1) Section 232(2) (voidness of provisions for indemnifying directors) does not apply to qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision.
@ref s 235(1) section 232(2) does not apply to qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision (src:3109-3109)
GIVEN `s 235(2) the provision is qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 235(1) the provision is permitted as qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 235(2) the provision is qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 232(2) ... does not apply to qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision" (it says nothing of other provision)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the provision qualifies is not known

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 236 Qualifying indemnity provision to be disclosed in directors' report
-- ======================================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 236(1) provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 236(1)(a) qualifying third party indemnity provision`
    `s 236(1)(b) qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision`
    `s 236(1) some other provision`

-- src:3127 | (1) This section requires disclosure in the directors' report of—
-- src:3128 | (a) qualifying third party indemnity provision, and
-- src:3129 | (b) qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision.
-- src:3130 | Such provision is referred to in this section as “qualifying indemnity provision”.
@ref s 236(1) qualifying indemnity provision (src:3127-3130)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 236(1) provision`
      `s 234(2) the provision is qualifying third party indemnity provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 235(2) the provision is qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(1) the provision is qualifying indemnity provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `s 236(1)(a) qualifying third party indemnity provision` THEN `s 234(2) the provision is qualifying third party indemnity provision`
    WHEN `s 236(1)(b) qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision` THEN `s 235(2) the provision is qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision`
    WHEN `s 236(1) some other provision` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) qualifying third party indemnity provision, and (b) qualifying pension scheme indemnity provision. Such provision is referred to in this section as “qualifying indemnity provision”"

DECLARE `s 236 when the provision is in force` IS ONE OF
    `s 236(2) when the directors' report is approved, for a director of the company`
    `s 236(3) at a time during the financial year, for a person then a director of the company`
    `s 236(4) when the directors' report is approved, provision made by the company for a director of an associated company`
    `s 236(5) at a time during the financial year, for a person then a director of an associated company`

-- src:3131 | (2) If when a directors' report is approved any qualifying indemnity provision (whether made by the company or otherwise) is in force for the benefit of one or more directors of the company, the report must state that such provision is in force.
-- src:3132 | (3) If at any time during the financial year to which a directors' report relates any such provision was in force for the benefit of one or more persons who were then directors of the company, the report must state that such provision was in force.
-- src:3133 | (4) If when a directors' report is approved qualifying indemnity provision made by the company is in force for the benefit of one or more directors of an associated company, the report must state that such provision is in force.
-- src:3134 | (5) If at any time during the financial year to which a directors' report relates any such provision was in force for the benefit of one or more persons who were then directors of an associated company, the report must state that such provision was in force.
@ref s 236(2) to (5) the report must state that the provision is in force (src:3131-3134)
GIVEN when IS A `s 236 when the provision is in force`
      `s 236(1) the provision is qualifying indemnity provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the provision is in force at that time for the benefit of one or more directors of the kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision was made by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236(2) to (5) the directors' report must state that the provision is in force or was in force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 236(1) the provision is qualifying indemnity provision` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the provision is qualifying indemnity provision is not known
        IF `s 236(1) the provision is qualifying indemnity provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any qualifying indemnity provision"
        IF NOT `the provision is in force at that time for the benefit of one or more directors of the kind`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If when a directors' report is approved any qualifying indemnity provision ... is in force for the benefit of one or more directors ..., the report must state that such provision is in force"
        IF (when EQUALS `s 236(4) when the directors' report is approved, provision made by the company for a director of an associated company` OR when EQUALS `s 236(5) at a time during the financial year, for a person then a director of an associated company`) AND (NOT `the provision was made by the company`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "qualifying indemnity provision made by the company is in force for the benefit of one or more directors of an associated company" (subsections (4) and (5) speak of provision made by the company)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:3131 | (2) If when a directors' report is approved any qualifying indemnity provision (whether made by the company or otherwise) is in force for the benefit of one or more directors of the company, the report must state that such provision is in force.
-- src:3132 | (3) If at any time during the financial year to which a directors' report relates any such provision was in force for the benefit of one or more persons who were then directors of the company, the report must state that such provision was in force.
-- src:3133 | (4) If when a directors' report is approved qualifying indemnity provision made by the company is in force for the benefit of one or more directors of an associated company, the report must state that such provision is in force.
-- src:3134 | (5) If at any time during the financial year to which a directors' report relates any such provision was in force for the benefit of one or more persons who were then directors of an associated company, the report must state that such provision was in force.
