         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the report must state that such provision is in force" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-MUST-1)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirement does not arise
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is not known to arise

